    "created_at": "2021-07-28T07:38:31Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-07-28T07:39:27Z",
    "body": "\"Can be omitted\" means that the element is created even when no start tag is encountered. Changing that parsing behavior isn't an option - it would break existing sites.\r\n\r\nThe \"Authors are encouraged...\" note is a non-normative recommendation which is present to address your concern. It also isn't _always_ the right thing to include `lang` in the source, though, given some documents change language dynamically or do not have a single dominant language and need more granular annotation (or may contain no text at all).",
