    "created_at": "2021-07-28T12:53:17Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-07-28T12:53:17Z",
    "body": "Some of the information in that document seems inaccurate:\r\n\r\n* User agents must obey `<meta http-equiv=content-language>`, that's not a \"can\".\r\n* The HTTP `Content-Language` response header is used to determine the language of a node, if other information is not available.\r\n\r\nOverall though I agree you ought to use the `lang` attribute.\r\n\r\nI don't think anything needs changing here though as per @bathos's comment.",
